    "description": "SEAL-KRETE Original is a clear, water-based waterproofing sealer for concrete and masonry, and it is a common sight in Menards' concrete aisle. It helps the surface shed water, which is the core goal on a Midwest concrete driveway, because water soaked into the top layer is what freezes and pops the surface off as scaling. The finish is clear and only lightly changes the look, and the label allows painting or coating over it later, which gives you flexibility if you plan to color the slab. For driveways that see heavy salt every winter, a dedicated silane-siloxane penetrating sealer offers stronger protection against chloride intrusion, so consider one if your slab is already showing scaling. Apply to clean, dry concrete that has cured for the period the label specifies, usually at least a month for new pours. Thin, even coats with a roller or pump sprayer work best; puddles dry cloudy. Expect to reapply every few years, sooner in tire tracks."
