        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Shopping for driveway sealer at Menards is really shopping for a Midwest winter. Choose flexible, polymer-modified, coal-tar-free asphalt sealers, fill frost-opened cracks before you seal, and work within the short warm season. Latex-ite Airport Grade is the balanced pick, BLACK JACK Drive-Maxx 1000 is the premium choice for neglected asphalt, and Rust-Oleum EPOXYSHIELD Blacktop is the budget option. Concrete driveways need SEAL-KRETE Original or a penetrating silane-siloxane instead.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Time a large order to a rebate period if you can, but do not buy so early that pails sit through a freeze. Seal in good weather, protect the coat from plows and salt, and fill new cracks every spring. That routine gets more years out of every pail than any label claim.
          </p>
